This is the **agent_bootstrap** repo — the source of truth for all AI agent configurations deployed across workspaces.

## Repo layout

- `skills/` — 35+ skill definitions (each has a SKILL.md)
- `rules/` — Cursor rule files (.mdc)
- `mcp/` — MCP server configs and docs
- `agents/` — Subagent definitions
- `commands/` — Command/prompt templates
- `hooks/` — Lifecycle hook scripts
- `manifest.json` — Tracks source plugin hashes and sync state
- `install.sh` — Deploys configs globally and per-workspace
- `sync.sh` — Detects and pulls updates from Cursor plugins and Codex skills

## When the user asks to update or sync this repo

1. Run `./sync.sh --check` first to show what's changed
2. If updates exist, run `./sync.sh --pull` to import them
3. Show the user `git diff` to review
4. Commit when asked: `git add -A && git commit -m 'sync: <description>'`
5. Optionally propagate: `./install.sh all ~/ATOM/`

## When the user asks to install or set up

- `./install.sh global` — global MCP, Codex skills, env var
- `./install.sh all ~/ATOM/` — all repos under ATOM
- `./install.sh workspace <path>` — single repo
- `./install.sh status` — show what's configured

## Available skills in this repo

You can read any skill at `skills/*/SKILL.md` to learn how to perform specialized tasks.
